    before: []  # bb64
    duplicate_of: []  # bb64
    not_duplicate_of: []  # bb64
    pr_ref:  # bb64
    description: "WI-tubot prospector run 2026-04-11 found that Airflow's openapi-gen TypeScript files produce large numbers of dead-code candidates — CancelablePromise.then, CancelablePromise.catch, request, path, process — all inside airflow-core/src/airflow/api_fastapi/auth/managers/simple/ui/openapi-gen/requests/core/. These are OpenAPI-generated TypeScript SDK stubs that should be flagged as is_generated_file=true and tier-demoted. WI-tizij (merged) added is_generated_file detection for Python v1alpha1_*/_pb2.py and Go zz_generated*/.pb.go, but not TypeScript openapi-gen output. Fix: extend is_generated_file heuristics to include paths containing '/openapi-gen/', filename patterns like 'ApiClient.ts', 'request.ts' within an openapi-gen directory, and file-header markers like '/* eslint-disable */ /* tslint:disable */' or '/* generated by OpenAPI' that are typical of openapi-codegen output. Scope: extend supply_chain.py or wherever is_generated_file is computed to include the TypeScript heuristic. Prospector evidence: ~200+ candidates per airflow run from openapi-gen paths alone. Related: WI-pofin (generalize @generated header detection) covers this pattern in more generality — could be handled there."  # bb64
    fields: {}  # bb64
